 build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \"DPBM contract\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \"applies\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, ACC, RI canary-onboarding instructions reference the DPBM contract layer. D-028 lands operationally once CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 have merged | ACCEPTED | DPBM closes a structural gap that pure-code lenses can't see — a frontend built under standard four-tier dispatch can satisfy every test and still drift from the design. Without an SCP-side adoption decision, agents working through SCP's MCP consult won't be told that the contract for visual-output work includes design artefacts. CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 (both 2026-04-28) introduce the upstream doctrine; SCP adopts at the policy layer. Full rationale + injection-mechanism specification in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:97:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections, and the restore-mode posture guard now fires on either empty `required_status_checks.contexts` or a non-canonical context set (both require an explicit acknowledgement flag); forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`, queries workflow-runs without a branch filter, validates `--expected-wrapper-sha` against actual release tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags/<tag>` with annotated-tag dereference fallback, and, when the adopter wrapper file is readable, verifies that `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` pins the same SHA before Gate 3 completes; inaccessible wrapper content now requires an explicit `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` acknowledgement rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure and explicitly names the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. After any break-glass cycle, `prior_restore_evidence_present` scans the full git history, so every subsequent forward-mode re-enable for the same adopter permanently requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` unless the operator deliberately takes the audited Gate 2 bypass; that permanence is intentional. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1207:- `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1209:- `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1210:- `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1248:    --expected-wrapper-sha <sha-from-Gate-2>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1251:When prior restore evidence exists, the helper requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` and validates that the SHA resolves to an actual release tag in the SCP repo. If the flag is omitted in that state, re-enable is rejected with exit 2.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1253:If the wrapper content cannot be read from the current context, the helper requires `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` before it will continue without wrapper-pin verification.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1255:> **Post-break-glass permanence:** After any break-glass cycle, all subsequent forward-mode `enable-required-check.sh` invocations for the same adopter permanently require `--expected-wrapper-sha` (or `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` with CAUTION audit). This is intentional: once an adopter has hit a break-glass, we demand operator-explicit SHA confirmation on every re-enable for the rest of the adopter's lifetime. The restore log entry in git history is the authoritative record; force-push to main is disabled (D-030) so the entry cannot be expunged.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1257:> **WARNING.** `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is an emergency-only bypass for Gate 2. It re-arms the gate against the current wrapper SHA, so if the wrapper is still pinned to a defective SCP SHA the gate will block adopters again.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1263:    --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1268:Reference: D-047, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
