 slice 024B at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04); after the operator-decided scope-split (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md), D-044 stays scoped to core deliverables; sibling D-NNN may be reserved at 024B-extras authoring time for the deferred surface (`--restore` + break-glass + workflow wiring). Slice 024B-core ships under documented protocol deviation per feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md note + justify rule (kernel hook lives in ACC repo only; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 - open). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge per the §9 reservation block. The original 024B accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 R-rounds against a single branch with each round closing 5-6 MAJ but introducing 2-3 new defects in just-added code (R6 missed primary-deliverable workflow wiring; R7 fix introduced bootstrap defect on slice's own PR). Empirical signal: surface area too large (16 files, ~3500 lines added) for single-pass convergence. Operator decided 2026-05-09 to split 024B into 024B-core (this slice; ~5 files; scaffolder + template + CI enforcement script + tests) + 024B-extras (deferred; `--restore` mode + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass + `.github/workflows/` CI wiring + step 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\n    97\t| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections, and the restore-mode posture guard now fires on either empty `required_status_checks.contexts` or a non-canonical context set (both require an explicit acknowledgement flag); forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`, queries workflow-runs without a branch filter, validates `--expected-wrapper-sha` against actual release tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags/<tag>` with annotated-tag dereference fallback, and, when the adopter wrapper file is readable, verifies that `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` pins the same SHA before Gate 3 completes; inaccessible wrapper content now requires an explicit `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` acknowledgement rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure and explicitly names the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. After any break-glass cycle, `prior_restore_evidence_present` scans the full git history, so every subsequent forward-mode re-enable for the same adopter permanently requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` unless the operator deliberately takes the audited Gate 2 bypass; that permanence is intentional. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\n    98\t\n    99\t> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
