{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba policies/VERSIONING.md | sed -n '80,100p; 260,285p'\"","aggregated_output":"    80\t- Promoting a rule from `threshold: warn` to `threshold: deny` as the **default** at the SCP source. (Adopters may always override per-rule via `.scp/rule-config.yaml`; the default flip is what's breaking.)\n    81\t- Tightening a rule's match scope such that previously-passing manifests now deny.\n    82\t\n    83\t### Read-back / annotation contracts\n    84\t\n    85\t- Removing `scp/policy-check-readback` commit-status posting.\n    86\t- Removing a `::warning::` or `::error::` annotation surface that adopters' downstream tooling parses (e.g. an annotation parser that grouped on `title=SCP-E001`).\n    87\t- Renaming an `SCP-ENNN` error-code identifier.\n    88\t\n    89\t### Branch-protection helper\n    90\t\n    91\t- Removing `--repo`, `--branch`, `--plan`, `--no-enforce-admins`, `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate`, `--restore`, `--expected-wrapper-sha`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions`, `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`, `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, or `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flags from `scripts/enable-required-check.sh`.\n    92\t- Changing the script's invocation-log markdown block schema.\n    93\t\n    94\t### Tag protection\n    95\t\n    96\t- Changing the `v*` or `renovate/v*` Repository Ruleset shape (deletion / non-fast-forward / update behaviour).\n    97\t\n    98\t---\n    99\t\n   100\t## What does NOT count as breaking\n   260\t  `policies/deprecations.yaml`.\n   261\t- The release-cut at v<X+1>.0.0 removes the rule from `policies/`\n   262\t  AND removes the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`. The\n   263\t  release-gate enforces this contract (refuses to cut the tag if\n   264\t  the entry is still present and the ramp window hasn't elapsed).\n   265\t- A migration pointer (link to a rule-proposal-style amending document\n   266\t  or a §M.N section of an ADR) MUST be in the warning annotation.\n   267\t\n   268\tNon-rule surfaces (workflow inputs, schema fields, annotation titles,\n   269\tbranch-protection helper flags, tag-protection patterns) follow the\n   270\tsame ramp pattern with surface-specific emission paths — the\n   271\t`policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `surface_kind` covering each\n   272\tcategory. The emission responsibility belongs to the surface\n   273\tmaintainer (e.g. a workflow-input deprecation announces via a\n   274\tdeprecation log line in the workflow itself).\n   275\t\n   276\t---\n   277\t\n   278\t## What \"stable\" means for v1.x\n   279\t\n   280\t`v1.0.0` (cut 2026-04-30) is the first stable release. Until v2.0.0 is\n   281\tcut:\n   282\t\n   283\t- The three rules `SCP-R-001`, `SCP-R-002`, `SCP-R-003` keep their IDs\n   284\t  and (subject to the deprecation ramp) their behaviour shape.\n   285\t- The `workflow_call` inputs declared on `policy-check.yml` at v1.0.0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
